# Auth & Permissions

## Auth State (`stores/authStore.ts`)

- `firebaseUser` — Firebase session
- `user` — backend `AppUser` with `people_id` and `person`
- `isGuest` — browse without login (no Firebase token)
- `ability` — CASL instance from `defineAbilityFor(person)`

Sign-in/sign-up flows must clear guest state (`isGuest: false`). Use `handleAuthStateChange` in `hooks/Auth/useAuthHandler.ts` after Firebase auth changes.

## secureFetch & Guests

- Authenticated: attaches `Authorization: Bearer <firebase id token>`
- Guest: no token; only endpoints marked `allowUnauthenticated` on backend
- Never create fake `Person` objects for guests

## CASL (`utils/casl/defineAbilityFor.ts`)

- Roles: Cell Leader, District Admin, People Admin, Member, Guest, etc.
- Subjects: `PeopleProfile`, `CellDetails`, `PeopleFlow`, `Announcements`, `Resource`, …
- Add new permissions here AND on backend; use `<Can action="..." subject="...">` in UI

## Firebase

- Use `@react-native-firebase/auth` (not web Firebase SDK)
- FCM token registration lives in root `app/_layout.tsx` — do not duplicate unless necessary
